jobResponsibilities:
TIER officers in the US Division are part of a dynamic and dedicated team responsible for advancing Singapore’s economic engagement with key markets and regional organisations in North America and Latin America, including the United States. You will work on creative and innovative initiatives with colleagues in MTI and our economic agencies that will develop your international economic perspectives, capabilities and experience by:

• Analysing and reporting on geostrategic developments and trends that affect the flows of goods, services, and investments;

• Formulating and refining strategies, policies and plans that enhance Singapore’s bilateral and plurilateral economic relations with the Americas, often in consultation and coordination with other ministries and agencies across the Whole-of-Government;

• Networking and developing connections with foreign government and business counterparts;

• Preparing and executing communications, consultations and engagements with key stakeholders in the business community and general public;

• Organising and representing MTI in visits, meetings, negotiations and conferences.

As a TIER officer in the Trade Strategy and Security Division, you will be part of a dynamic team working on fast-moving pieces to help Singapore navigate changes in our geo-economic environment. You will have the opportunity to hone your strategic thinking skillset, policy acumen, and international orientation perspectives in both the economic and security domains, by:

•	Assessing the impact and implications of geo-political developments on Singapore’s economic and security interests;

•	Developing strategies, policies, options and responses to expand Singapore’s economic heft or relevance as well as strengthen Singapore’s economic resilience;

•	Preparing and executing communications and engagement strategies with key public and private sector stakeholders;

•	Organising and representing MTI at various high-level inter-agency platforms related to economic, security, and geo-political portfolios; and

•	Collaborating and networking with various internal and external stakeholders.

